      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T21:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually now looking at the [SkCodec getFrameInfo documentation](https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/third_party/skia/HEAD/include/codec/SkCodec.h;l\u003d753?q\u003dSkCodec) more closely:\n\n\u003e To elaborate, some codecs support animation (e.g. GIF). Others do not (e.g. BMP). Animated codecs can still represent single frame images. Calling getFrameInfo(0, etc) will return true for a single frame GIF even if the overall image is not animated.\n\nSo I think this behavior was intended, and it makes sense as the frame also has meaningful metadata that may be worth looking at even for a static image.\n\nIt doesn’t seem like this behavior matters for AOSP, I sent this CL because I noticed the `Codec_frames` test failing when working on the CL to disable APNG in AOSP and realized the failure was at head.\n\nSo I think the issue is actually with the `Codec_frames` test here, seems like the test should be updated. I’ll update the CL to do that instead.",
